 NotifyGatekeeper packageID;rc;msg;qdmx
⍝ Tells the gatekeeper(s) that `packageID` has been published. Whether an email is sent at
⍝ all is decided by `Emails.SendMail_PublishedPkg`.
⍝ `SavePackage` runs this as a thread, and that is what the function is for: an SMTP server
⍝ may take tens of seconds to answer, or never answer at all, and until it does the client
⍝ has no response. Plodder closes the connection as idle long before that, the client cannot
⍝ tell that from a request that never arrived and sends the same one again, and the server
⍝ reports the package it has just written as already published.
⍝ A thread has no caller for an error to travel to, so this one reports for itself. It traps
⍝ whatever `SendMail` may throw as well: a suspended thread would sit in the server for the
⍝ rest of its life, holding on to a Conga client.
 :Trap 0
     (rc msg)←Emails.SendMail_PublishedPkg G.INI packageID G.RegistryPath
 :Else
     qdmx←⎕DMX
     (rc msg)←qdmx.EN qdmx.EM
 :EndTrap
 :If rc≠0
     LogError'Sending email to gatekeeper with notification of a published package failed: ',(⍕rc),'; ',⍕∊msg
 :EndIf
⍝Done
